1.4.m:
Sanaka said:
All religious duties preceded by faith yield the fruit of one’s desires;
everything is accomplished through faith; Hari is pleased through faith.

1.8.s:
// sāgara uvāca
bho bho guro durācārānetānrakṣasi tānvṛthā /
sarvathāhaṃ haniṣyāmi matpiturdeśahārakān //

1.8.m:
Aurva said:
One shall bear a single continuer of the lineage, and the other sixty thousand;
O fortunate ladies, choose according to your desire for offspring!

Aṃśumat said:
"O sage, whatever bad conduct was committed by my uncles, forgive that;
for the virtuous are devoted to helping others, and their essence is forbearance.
